# RBAC permissions (canonical registry)

**SSOT:** [`shared/rbac/permission-registry.json`](shared/rbac/permission-registry.json)

Generated artifacts (checked in, never hand-edited):

- Rust: [`src-tauri/src/rbac/permissions_generated.rs`](src-tauri/src/rbac/permissions_generated.rs) via `crate::rbac::permissions::*`
- TypeScript: [`shared/rbac/permissions.generated.ts`](shared/rbac/permissions.generated.ts) via `P.*` / `PermissionName`

## Hard rules

1. **Never** write permission names as string literals (`"inv.procure"`, `'ot.edit'`, etc.) in app code, tests, seeders, or docs-as-code that gates behavior.
2. Backend enforcement must use `crate::rbac::permissions::CONST` (or re-exports of those constants).
3. Frontend gates must use `P.CONST` / `PermissionName` from the generated module.
4. Every registry entry must declare intentional `usage`: `backend` | `frontend` | `both` | `catalog-only` (catalog-only requires `usage_justification`).
5. After changing the registry, run `pnpm rbac:generate` then `pnpm rbac:check`.
6. CI must fail when: generated files are stale, an enforced permission is missing from the registry, a registry entry lacks intentional usage / has no matching references when usage requires them, or a forbidden permission literal appears outside the allowlist.

## Workflow

```text
1. Edit shared/rbac/permission-registry.json only
2. pnpm rbac:generate
3. Use new P.* / permissions::* constants at call sites
4. pnpm rbac:check
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<PermissionGate permission="inv.procure">…</PermissionGate>
can("ot.close")

// ✅ GOOD
import { P } from "@shared/rbac/permissions.generated";
<PermissionGate permission={P.INV_PROCURE}>…</PermissionGate>
can(P.OT_CLOSE)
```

```rust
// ❌ BAD
require_permission!(state, &user, "eq.manage", PermissionScope::Global);

// ✅ GOOD
require_permission!(state, &user, crate::rbac::permissions::EQ_MANAGE, PermissionScope::Global);
```

VPS/control-plane policy strings (`license.runtime`, `sync.runtime`, `platform.health`) are **not** desktop RBAC and must stay out of this registry.
